<h2>Indian cardamom for export</h2>
<p>Small green cardamom from Kerala's Idukki hills is India's highest-value spice export per kilogram, and the trade is overwhelmingly Gulf-facing. We supply size-graded cardamom — from bold 8mm+ export grade down through AGEB, AGS and smaller commercial grades — sourced from Kerala, Karnataka's Kodagu and Chikmagalur belts, and Tamil Nadu.</p>

<p>Cardamom harvest doesn't follow a single window the way most spices do. Pods on the same plant mature at different times, so pickers work the plantations in repeated staggered rounds from roughly August through February, which spreads fresh supply over a longer season than most of our other products.</p>

<h2>How should I specify cardamom?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Size grade.</strong> Bold 8mm+ pods command the top price and are typically what premium retail and Gulf food-service buyers specify. AGEB, AGS and smaller grades cost less and suit bulk or industrial use.</li>
  <li><strong>Colour.</strong> Deep green is generally preferred and commands a premium over paler, less-vivid pods of the same size grade.</li>
  <li><strong>Storage sensitivity.</strong> Cardamom loses aroma faster than most spices — confirm your packaging and transit plan protects against heat and light exposure, especially for long sea-freight routes.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Which markets buy Indian cardamom?</h2>
<p>The Gulf dominates this trade to a degree unmatched by any other spice we handle — the UAE and Saudi Arabia alone are roughly 61% of India's export value, with Kuwait, Iraq and Oman extending that further. See the full cited breakdown below.</p>

<h2>Cardamom export pricing</h2>
<p>Cardamom is priced per kilogram at a level well above other commodity spices, and size/colour grade moves price materially. Send your target grade, quantity and destination port and we'll quote current FOB/CIF terms.</p>

